  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONS OF STRATEGIC PROPERTIES IN QUEBEC&apos;S</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Atlantic Northern Forest contains a wealth of natural resources, but these resources also face numerous threats: over 90% of the area is in private hands. Located within an hour&apos;s drive of Montreal, the largest city in Quebec, the pressure on the region&apos;s natural habitats for residential development, recreational activities and infrastructures is considerable. This project will protect in perpetuity 1,000 acres through either fee-simple or easement acquisition. Located in Quebec&apos;s Northern Green Mountains natural trans-border corridor, the targeted properties are strategically located in core areas of unfragmented forest, and form a crucial link maintaining connectivity between properties already protected in the region. The project will also build capacity with grantee partners, who carry out related work in the area...Species that will benefit include: peregrine falcon, wood thrush, Canada warbler, eastern wood-pewee, veery, yellow-bellied sapsucker, black-throated green warbler, black-throated blue warbler, ovenbird, northern flicker, broad-winged hawk, belted kingfisher, American bittern, American black duck, and ..</narrative>
  </description>
